# concept DOI from `doi:` once the first release is archived on Zenodo.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "BeeSensor"
abstract: >-
  BeeSensor (Saleem, Ullah & Farooq, 2012), the honeybee-inspired energy-aware
  routing protocol for wireless sensor networks, as a standalone swarm routing
  protocol: many-to-one convergecast to a sink, planned as a
  simulator-agnostic C++ core and an ns-3 contrib module on swarm-core, with a
  paper-fidelity sheet.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Joppi
    given-names: Daniel Henrique
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6436-8174"
version: "0.0.0"
# The work as a whole; core/ also MIT OR GPL-2.0-only (LICENSING.md).
